WEBVTT

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:02.900
Are you a SMART fella,

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.933
or a FART smella?

00:00:04.933 --> 00:00:06.433
Let's find OUT!

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:08.233
Okay!

00:00:08.233 --> 00:00:11.433
Which one does NOT belong?

00:00:11.433 --> 00:00:12.067
A.

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:12.733
Rose,

00:00:12.733 --> 00:00:13.367
B.

00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:14.000
Oak,

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:14.633
C.

00:00:14.633 --> 00:00:15.267
Tulip,

00:00:15.267 --> 00:00:16.567
or D.

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:17.200
Daisy?

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.467
Five seconds!

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:25.467
TIME'S UP!

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:27.333
The answer is...

00:00:27.333 --> 00:00:27.733
B,

00:00:27.733 --> 00:00:28.133
oak!

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:28.933
A rose,

00:00:28.933 --> 00:00:29.333
tulip,

00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:31.333
and daisy are all flowers.

00:00:31.333 --> 00:00:33.333
An oak is a tree,

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.333
so it does not belong.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:37.567
Here's one,

00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:39.133
a picture puzzle!

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:41.800
Which shape completes the pattern?

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:42.333
A.

00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:43.900
A filled square,

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:44.433
B.

00:00:44.433 --> 00:00:46.033
A filled triangle,

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:46.567
C.

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:48.167
An empty circle,

00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:49.200
or D.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.800
A filled circle?

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:51.867
Five seconds!

00:00:57.633 --> 00:00:58.833
TIME'S UP!

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:00.700
The answer is...

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:01.100
D,

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:02.300
a filled circle!

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.700
The rule is the shape gets

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:07.100
filled in but stays the same

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:07.500
shape,

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.900
so the empty circle becomes a

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:10.700
filled circle.

00:01:11.867 --> 00:01:13.067
Here's one,

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:14.900
a number series!

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:15.500
Four,

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:16.100
five,

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:16.700
seven,

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:17.333
ten,

00:01:17.333 --> 00:01:17.933
fourteen,

00:01:17.933 --> 00:01:19.133
and then...

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:20.967
what comes next?

00:01:20.967 --> 00:01:21.567
A.

00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:22.167
Eighteen,

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:22.767
B.

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:23.400
Nineteen,

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:24.000
C.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:24.600
Twenty,

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:25.800
or D.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:26.400
Seventeen?

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.633
Five seconds!

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.600
TIME'S UP!

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:36.933
The answer is...

00:01:36.933 --> 00:01:37.467
B,

00:01:37.467 --> 00:01:38.033
nineteen!

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:40.800
The gaps grow by one:

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:41.900
plus one,

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:42.467
two,

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:43.000
three,

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:43.567
four,

00:01:43.567 --> 00:01:45.233
then plus five.

00:01:45.233 --> 00:01:48.533
So fourteen plus five is nineteen.

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:50.100
So,

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.133
are you smart or fart?

00:01:52.133 --> 00:01:54.567
Count up your correct answers to

00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:55.767
find your rank!

00:01:56.933 --> 00:01:57.267
So,

00:01:57.267 --> 00:01:58.667
how did you do?

00:01:58.667 --> 00:02:00.033
Comment your score below,

00:02:00.033 --> 00:02:01.400
and follow for more!
